# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for Ajit-backprop-test (Python 3.13 project)
# =============================================================================
# Per Agent Action Plan (AAP) §0.5.1 and §0.3.2, this file enumerates ignore
# patterns appropriate for a Python 3.13 project. It supersedes any prior
# Node-based .gitignore. Build artifacts, virtual environments, tool caches,
# secret material (.env), and IDE-specific scratch files are excluded from
# version control. Defensive Node/JS patterns are also included so that an
# accidental npm/yarn invocation does not pollute the repository.
#
# Pattern discipline:
#   - Trailing-slash patterns (e.g. `dist/`) match directories only.
#   - Bare patterns (e.g. `.coverage`) match files or directories of that name.
#   - Wildcards follow git's gitignore syntax (man gitignore).
#   - Negation rules (`!path`) re-include files matched by an earlier pattern.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1: Python Bytecode and Compilation Artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CPython 3.13 writes compiled bytecode into `__pycache__` directories and
# `*.pyc`/`*.pyo` files. Jython writes `*$py.class`. None of these belong in
# version control because they are reproducible from the source `*.py`.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2: Distribution and Packaging
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outputs of `python -m build`, `setup.py`, and pip's local installation
# scratch space. Per AAP §0.3.2, build artifacts are explicitly out of scope
# and must not be committed.
.Python
build/
dist/
sdist/
develop-eggs/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
var/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
MANIFEST

# pip / setuptools intermediate files
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Wheel build outputs
share/python-wheels/
wheels/

# PyInstaller manifests (only useful at distribution time)
*.manifest
*.spec


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3: Virtual Environments and Secrets
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments are local to each developer's machine and must never
# be committed (AAP §0.5.1). The Setup Status Log confirms the project's
# venv lives at `.venv/`.
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.virtualenv/

# CRITICAL (AAP §0.8.2): the ACTUAL `.env` file (containing real DB_HOST,
# API_KEY, and other secret values) MUST NEVER be committed. Only the
# `.env.example` template (containing blank placeholders) is committed —
# the negation pattern below explicitly preserves it even though gitignore
# semantics already exclude `.env.example` from the `.env` rule.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.staging
.env.production
.env.test
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# direnv local environment
.envrc


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4: Test Artifacts and Coverage Reports
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per AAP §0.5.1: `.pytest_cache/`, `.coverage`, `htmlcov/` are ignored.
# Coverage XML/JSON outputs and Hypothesis databases are likewise local
# scratch files that should be regenerated on each test run.
.pytest_cache/
.cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
*.cover
*.py,cover
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# JUnit / xUnit XML test reports
nose2-junit.xml
junit.xml
junit/
test-results/
report.xml


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 5: Type Checker and Linter Caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per AAP §0.5.1: `.mypy_cache/` and `.ruff_cache/` are ignored. Other type
# checkers (Pyre, Pytype) and the mypy daemon (dmypy) also write local caches.
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
.ruff_cache/
.pylint.d/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 6: IDE and Editor Scratch Files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workspace-specific configuration that varies between developers. Teams
# that wish to share specific editor settings (e.g., `.vscode/settings.json`)
# can selectively un-ignore them with `!` rules below this block.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.project
.pydevproject
.settings/
.spyderproject
.spyproject
.ropeproject

# Vim / Emacs / nano swap and backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo

# OS-specific metadata
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 7: Tool Caches, Logs, and Local Overrides
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generic log files, local Django/Flask overrides, and pipenv lock files for
# tools the project does not adopt. Note: `poetry.lock` and `uv.lock` are
# intentionally NOT ignored — they may be committed if those tools are used
# for supplementary lockfile generation alongside `requirements.txt`
# (AAP §0.6.1 mentions `uv` as an optional faster installer).
*.log
*.log.*
logs/
local_settings.py
instance/
.webassets-cache

# Pipenv (project uses pip + requirements.txt, not pipenv)
Pipfile.lock

# Celery beat schedule
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# SageMath parsed files
*.sage.py

# IPython / Jupyter notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/
profile_default/
ipython_config.py


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 8: Documentation Build Artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sphinx, MkDocs, and similar generators write into local build folders that
# must not be committed (the canonical source is the .md / .rst input).
docs/_build/
docs/build/
docs/_static/
docs/_templates/_build/
.sphinx-build/
site/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 9: Containers and Deployment Runtime Artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Process IDs, Unix domain sockets, and other runtime byproducts.
*.pid
*.sock
*.seed
*.pid.lock


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 10: Local Database and Migration Artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local SQLite databases used during development. Production data and
# Alembic-generated migration files are NOT ignored — only ad-hoc local
# database files are. (Alembic migration scripts under
# `src/ajit_backprop/db/migrations/` are first-class source and committed.)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 11: Defensive Ignore — JavaScript / Node.js Era Artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per AAP §0.3.2, the project does not use Node.js. These patterns are
# defensive: if any JS tool is ever invoked accidentally (or if a
# contributor experiments with the source archive at `society_mgmt_300k.zip`),
# the resulting Node-specific files will be ignored automatically.
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
bower_components/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
yarn.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnp.*

# Bundler / transpiler outputs (also Node-era; defensive)
.next/
.nuxt/
.parcel-cache/
.cache-loader/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 12: Miscellaneous Local Tooling and Editor Plugins
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pre-commit local cache, mypy daemon socket, and other transient files.
.pre-commit-cache/

# Local Docker overrides (production docker-compose.yml is committed; only
# developer-specific override files are ignored)
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# Profiler outputs (per AAP §0.7.2 profiling protocol — `cProfile` writes
# to local files that are scratch artifacts and not source)
*.prof
*.pstats
profile.out

# Backup files from migration/refactor scripts
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Local archive expansions (e.g., `society_mgmt_300k_extracted/` — the .zip
# itself remains tracked per the current repository state, but any local
# extraction directory is scratch space)
society_mgmt_300k_extracted/
